				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<h5 class="elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default">Frequently asked Questions</h5>				</div>
				</div>
				<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-aa0f22c elementor-widget elementor-widget-accordion" data-id="aa0f22c" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="accordion.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
							<div class="elementor-accordion">
							<div class="elementor-accordion-item">
					<div id="elementor-tab-title-1781" class="elementor-tab-title" data-tab="1" role="button" aria-controls="elementor-tab-content-1781" aria-expanded="false">
													<span class="elementor-accordion-icon elementor-accordion-icon-left" aria-hidden="true">
															<span class="elementor-accordion-icon-closed"><svg class="e-font-icon-svg e-fas-plus" viewBox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span>
								<span class="elementor-accordion-icon-opened"><svg class="e-font-icon-svg e-fas-minus" viewBox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h384c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span>
														</span>
												<a class="elementor-accordion-title" tabindex="0">What is the main purpose of yoga?</a>
					</div>
					<div id="elementor-tab-content-1781" class="elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix" data-tab="1" role="region" aria-labelledby="elementor-tab-title-1781"><p>The main purpose of yoga is to cultivate physical, mental, and spiritual well-being through a holistic practice that integrates breath control, meditation, and physical postures. By harmonizing the body, mind, and spirit, yoga aims to promote balance, flexibility, strength, and inner peace. Beyond the physical benefits, yoga encourages self-awareness, mindfulness, and connection to the present moment, fostering a sense of unity with oneself and the surrounding world. Ultimately, yoga serves as a path to self-discovery, personal growth, and overall fulfillment.</p></div>
				</div>
							<div class="elementor-accordion-item">
					<div id="elementor-tab-title-1782" class="elementor-tab-title" data-tab="2" role="button" aria-controls="elementor-tab-content-1782" aria-expanded="false">
													<span class="elementor-accordion-icon elementor-accordion-icon-left" aria-hidden="true">
															<span class="elementor-accordion-icon-closed"><svg class="e-font-icon-svg e-fas-plus" viewBox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span>
								<span class="elementor-accordion-icon-opened"><svg class="e-font-icon-svg e-fas-minus" viewBox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h384c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span>
														</span>
												<a class="elementor-accordion-title" tabindex="0">What is yoga and the benefits?</a>
					</div>
					<div id="elementor-tab-content-1782" class="elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix" data-tab="2" role="region" aria-labelledby="elementor-tab-title-1782"><p>Yoga is a holistic practice originating from ancient India that integrates physical postures, breath control, meditation, and philosophical principles. It promotes overall health and well-being by improving flexibility, strength, and balance. Additionally, yoga reduces stress, enhances mental clarity, and fosters emotional balance. Regular practice can also improve posture, increase energy levels, and cultivate a deeper sense of self-awareness and inner peace, making it a valuable tool for holistic wellness in today&#8217;s fast-paced world.</p></div>
				</div>
							<div class="elementor-accordion-item">
					<div id="elementor-tab-title-1783" class="elementor-tab-title" data-tab="3" role="button" aria-controls="elementor-tab-content-1783" aria-expanded="false">
													<span class="elementor-accordion-icon elementor-accordion-icon-left" aria-hidden="true">
															<span class="elementor-accordion-icon-closed"><svg class="e-font-icon-svg e-fas-plus" viewBox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span>
								<span class="elementor-accordion-icon-opened"><svg class="e-font-icon-svg e-fas-minus" viewBox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h384c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span>
														</span>
												<a class="elementor-accordion-title" tabindex="0">What is the full form of YOGA?</a>
					</div>
					<div id="elementor-tab-content-1783" class="elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix" data-tab="3" role="region" aria-labelledby="elementor-tab-title-1783"><p>The full form of yoga is derived from the Sanskrit word &#8220;Yuj,&#8221; meaning to unite or yoke. Thus, the full form of yoga can be understood as &#8220;union&#8221; or &#8220;integration&#8221; of body, mind, and spirit. Yoga encompasses various practices, including physical postures (asanas), breath control (pranayama), meditation, and philosophical principles, all aimed at achieving harmony and balance within oneself and with the surrounding world. Through yoga, individuals seek to unite their individual consciousness with the universal consciousness, fostering holistic well-being and spiritual growth.</p></div>
				</div>
							<div class="elementor-accordion-item">
					<div id="elementor-tab-title-1784" class="elementor-tab-title" data-tab="4" role="button" aria-controls="elementor-tab-content-1784" aria-expanded="false">
													<span class="elementor-accordion-icon elementor-accordion-icon-left" aria-hidden="true">
															<span class="elementor-accordion-icon-closed"><svg class="e-font-icon-svg e-fas-plus" viewBox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span>
								<span class="elementor-accordion-icon-opened"><svg class="e-font-icon-svg e-fas-minus" viewBox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h384c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span>
														</span>
												<a class="elementor-accordion-title" tabindex="0">Who is the father of yoga?</a>
					</div>
					<div id="elementor-tab-content-1784" class="elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix" data-tab="4" role="region" aria-labelledby="elementor-tab-title-1784"><p>The father of yoga is often credited to be Patanjali, an ancient Indian sage who compiled the Yoga Sutras, a foundational text on the philosophy and practice of yoga. Patanjali&#8217;s Yoga Sutras, written around 400 CE, outline the eight limbs of yoga, including ethical principles, physical postures (asanas), breath control (pranayama), and meditation techniques. His teachings have had a profound influence on the development and spread of yoga as a spiritual and holistic practice worldwide.</p></div>
				</div>
							<div class="elementor-accordion-item">
					<div id="elementor-tab-title-1785" class="elementor-tab-title" data-tab="5" role="button" aria-controls="elementor-tab-content-1785" aria-expanded="false">
													<span class="elementor-accordion-icon elementor-accordion-icon-left" aria-hidden="true">
															<span class="elementor-accordion-icon-closed"><svg class="e-font-icon-svg e-fas-plus" viewBox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span>
								<span class="elementor-accordion-icon-opened"><svg class="e-font-icon-svg e-fas-minus" viewBox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h384c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span>
														</span>
												<a class="elementor-accordion-title" tabindex="0">Which yoga is most important?</a>
					</div>
					<div id="elementor-tab-content-1785" class="elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix" data-tab="5" role="region" aria-labelledby="elementor-tab-title-1785"><p>It&#8217;s challenging to label one specific type of yoga as the most important, as each style offers unique benefits suited to individual needs and preferences. However, Hatha yoga is often considered foundational, focusing on physical postures (asanas) and breath control (pranayama) to achieve balance and alignment. It provides a solid framework for beginners to build strength, flexibility, and mindfulness, serving as a gateway to explore other yoga styles and deepen one&#8217;s practice.</p></div>
				</div>
							<div class="elementor-accordion-item">
					<div id="elementor-tab-title-1786" class="elementor-tab-title" data-tab="6" role="button" aria-controls="elementor-tab-content-1786" aria-expanded="false">
													<span class="elementor-accordion-icon elementor-accordion-icon-left" aria-hidden="true">
															<span class="elementor-accordion-icon-closed"><svg class="e-font-icon-svg e-fas-plus" viewBox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span>
								<span class="elementor-accordion-icon-opened"><svg class="e-font-icon-svg e-fas-minus" viewBox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h384c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span>
														</span>
												<a class="elementor-accordion-title" tabindex="0">Who is the king of yoga?</a>
					</div>
					<div id="elementor-tab-content-1786" class="elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix" data-tab="6" role="region" aria-labelledby="elementor-tab-title-1786"><p>In the realm of yoga, there is no singular &#8220;king,&#8221; as yoga is a diverse practice with many influential figures throughout history. However, if we were to highlight one prominent figure, it would be Patanjali. Patanjali is revered for his compilation of the Yoga Sutras, a foundational text that outlines the principles and philosophy of yoga. His teachings continue to guide and inspire practitioners worldwide, earning him a respected place in the yoga community.</p></div>
				</div>
							<div class="elementor-accordion-item">
					<div id="elementor-tab-title-1787" class="elementor-tab-title" data-tab="7" role="button" aria-controls="elementor-tab-content-1787" aria-expanded="false">
													<span class="elementor-accordion-icon elementor-accordion-icon-left" aria-hidden="true">
															<span class="elementor-accordion-icon-closed"><svg class="e-font-icon-svg e-fas-plus" viewBox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span>
								<span class="elementor-accordion-icon-opened"><svg class="e-font-icon-svg e-fas-minus" viewBox="0 0 448 512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M416 208H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h384c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z"></path></svg></span>
														</span>
												<a class="elementor-accordion-title" tabindex="0">Who named yoga?</a>
					</div>
					<div id="elementor-tab-content-1787" class="elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix" data-tab="7" role="region" aria-labelledby="elementor-tab-title-1787"><p>The term &#8220;yoga&#8221; originated from ancient Sanskrit and is derived from the root word &#8220;yuj,&#8221; meaning &#8220;to yoke&#8221; or &#8220;to unite.&#8221; The name &#8220;yoga&#8221; was not given by any individual but evolved over thousands of years through the teachings and practices of ancient Indian sages and scholars. It encompasses a wide range of physical, mental, and spiritual disciplines aimed at achieving harmony, balance, and union between the body, mind, and spirit.</p></div>
				</div>
								</div>
						</div>
				</div>
